    ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4959",
    ":question/problem": "Express $\\sqrt[5]{4}$ using a fractional exponent.",
    ":question/worked-solution": "The radical $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ can be written using a fractional exponent as $x^{1/n}.$\n\nComparing $\\sqrt[n]{x}$ with $\\sqrt[5]{4},$ we get $x = 4$ and $n = 5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[5]{4} = 4^{1/5}.\n$$"
  },
